<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="intro-inference">
  <title>Introduction to Statistical Inference</title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter introduces statistical inference. For the main ideas, see
      <xref ref="sec-parameters-and-estimates"/>, <xref ref="sec-bayesian-statistics"/>,
      <xref ref="sec-election-forecasting"/>, and <xref ref="sec-bootstrap"/>. For an applied example of
      uncertainty quantification in public forecasting, see FiveThirtyEight's explanation of its election
      forecast <url href="https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/how-fivethirtyeights-election-forecast-works/">online</url>.
    </p>
  </introduction>

</chapter>
